window.EN={"1":"Having come through the forest, Leif's \"Liberation Army\" at last reaches the south gate of Leonster.","2":"But even the south gate, which should have been thinly held, was protected by high cliffs and numerous shooters,","3":"and was in a state that could not easily be approached.","4":"Prince, Leonster Castle is in sight. This is the back side, so the enemy will be off their guard.","5":"But August, the east side is all cliffs; we can't reach the castle.","6":"If we circle around from the west, the shooters will pick us off. What on earth do you intend to do?","7":"Indeed... That there would be so many ballista units is beyond what I expected.","8":"That said, if we dawdle, enemy reinforcements will appear. This is a difficulty...","9":"Dorias, your opinion?","10":"Unless we take out the shooters, advancing is impossible. Send people in by magic, or attack from the sky...","11":"Either way, we must be prepared for some sacrifices.","12":"Understood. Let me think whether there's some good way.","13":"General Amalda, for someone of your standing to be assigned to guard the back gate... what on earth happened?","14":"It seems my opinion offended Marquis Gustav...","15":"The matter of the child hunts. Did you argue again?","16":"Marquis Gustav, without any order from the King, is taking children from the villages around here.","17":"He means to make them offerings to the Loptr Church.","18":"Do you think such a thing should be allowed?","19":"Now, now, Lady Amalda.","20":"I understand how you feel, but the gathering of children is something Emperor Arvis himself has assented to.","21":"Sooner or later the children around here will all be taken away to the capital. Your opposing it alone will change nothing.","22":"Kh, how did it come to this!!","23":"I believed in Emperor Arvis. I became a soldier because I admired him. What on earth has become of him?","24":"Hey, been waiting for you. I've heard the story from the boss. Well, good luck.","25":"The castle is in danger... All troops, we now go to its relief. Don't fall behind the rebels!","26":"Ahh... Lord Leif... How good of you to return.","27":"How long we, the people of Leonster, have waited for this day...","28":"Village head... and everyone in the village, I'm sorry for making you suffer for so long.","29":"But it's all right now.","30":"We now head to retake the castle with the full strength of the Leonster knights. I want you to believe in our victory.","31":"Prince, I have a request. Please let us help with the advance on the castle too.","32":"Help... You're saying the villagers will fight?","33":"Yes. Until now we have endured every abuse from the Empire.","34":"But thinking that someday, surely, our homeland would be liberated, we secretly gathered weapons and prepared.","35":"But village head, they say there are many ballistae inside the castle.","36":"Militia without proper equipment will be picked off.","37":"Naturally, we do not expect to come back alive. It is enough if we can become the prince's shield.","38":"We will draw the ballistae. Meanwhile, Prince, take the castle...","39":"Absurd! What is victory for, if we lose you! I won't allow such a thing!","40":"Lord Leif... Do you know how much we have suffered these ten-odd years?","41":"Our young daughters were taken by the lord, Gustav; our children were taken by the Loptr Church.","42":"Those who resisted were treated with real cruelty and killed along with their families.","43":"Prince... the weak, such as we, cannot live if we lose our country.","44":"So if the country can be regained, we will cooperate in anything whatsoever.","45":"Our lives we do not begrudge in the least.","46":"Village head...","47":"Prince Leif, do you understand? When a country falls, the most pitiable are the people left behind.","48":"They are not saying they will die out of the cheap sort of loyalty knights speak of.","49":"You must not trample on their feelings with childish sentimentality.","50":"...August, are you saying I should ask for their cooperation!?","51":"I am saying that is one way.","52":"Dorias, your opinion?","53":"It is not that I can't understand the villagers' feelings, but I am still opposed.","54":"But in any case, it is for you to judge, Lord Leif.","55":"What shall we do? → Have the residents cooperate / Attack by our own strength","56":"You're with the Leonster army, aren't you? Where might Lord Leif be?","57":"Hey, you folks. You're attacking Leonster Castle, right? I've got a tip worth hearing...","58":"Truth is, there's a little trick to the east gate of that castle.","59":"It's rigged so that if we just work it a bit, the gate opens.","60":"How about it? Care to make use of us?","61":"Of course it won't be free. Something along the lines of you stacking up 20000G...","62":"What, expensive? Don't be stupid. We're risking our lives too. We've got to get that much.","63":"If you don't want to, fine. What'll it be? → Pay 20000G / That's a waste; attack from the front","64":"What's this, what's this. I've got no business with folks who have no money. Go on, get out of here.","65":"We've finally reached the castle gate. What is the situation inside?","66":"August, tell me the information you've gathered.","67":"Sir...","68":"The castle's commander is a man named Gustav, a close aide of King Bloom. A man with a great many problems.","69":"Marquis Gustav... The man who, as lord of Leonster these ten-odd years, has committed every kind of tyranny...","70":"Indeed. As a commander he is second-rate,","71":"but having spared no expense, he is equipped with excellent arms and armor, so he may be quite a tough foe.","72":"What else...?","73":"The problem is General Xavier.","74":"He appears to be quite the warrior, and the heavy knights under him are thought to be considerable men as well.","75":"Xavier, you say! Kh... that traitor!!!","76":"Dorias...? Do you know him?","77":"Sir...","78":"It is shameful to say, but Xavier was once a general of Leonster.","79":"Everyone trusted him as a man of honor,","80":"but the moment Leonster fell, he turned his coat and went over to the enemy!","81":"I cannot forgive him! That shameless wretch I will bring down with my own hands, without fail!!","82":"Lord Dorias!! That is not so!","83":"Village head...? What are you saying? Do you mean to defend a traitor!","84":"It is not that. General Xavier surrendered against his will, in order to protect us.","85":"The country had fallen, and we common folk were left behind in the midst of the enemy.","86":"The general took pity on us, and saved us in exchange for his own honor.","87":"Had the general not been here, we could not have survived.","88":"What!... Is that true!!","89":"But if so, why does he still sit idle now that the prince has returned?","90":"If he led the soldiers under him and raised a revolt inside the castle, the castle could easily be taken...","91":"Well... the general has eight adjutants who have shared his joys and sorrows,","92":"and their wives and children are held hostage inside the castle.","93":"Even the general can do nothing without those adjutants' consent.","94":"After all, he is a kind man who cares for his subordinates...","95":"Then if we rescue those hostages, the general will be freed!!","96":"But it will not be so easy...","97":"I must apologize to the general. As the surviving royal, I have to ask his forgiveness!","98":"Then, Lord Leif, please take this from us.","99":"This is a Knight Proof... a knight's crest.","100":"Yes. Since we could be of no help in taking the castle,","101":"we thought at least this much, and brought it.","102":"Thank you, village head. Please give my regards to everyone in the village.","103":"When you retake the castle, Lord Leif, you will formally become \"Prince.\"","104":"Given the times, it cannot be a grand ceremony,","105":"but all the people are looking forward to seeing you in your glory, Prince.","106":"I will not hand this castle to the likes of you!","107":"...Friege... is far away...","108":"I can no longer live as a soldier. I'll go back home for now...","109":"What on earth am I doing...","110":"This is fine... For me... covered in blood... an unsightly end is what's fitting...","111":"So I must see more of this nightmare..."};
